  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Oil Wealth and Development in Uganda and Beyond (2019), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 4 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 5,201 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Oil Wealth and Development in Uganda and Beyond by Arnim Langer and Ukoha Ukiwo was published by Leuven University Press in 2019. Conceptually, the work connects to Economics and Business.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 4 citations. Citations peaked in 2023 with 2 citing works. Notable citing venues include Climate Policy, African Studies Review and Political Science Research and Methods. The citing works include 3 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 6 countries, led by France, the United States and Brazil.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 5,201 times via OAPEN. It is recorded in 1 library collection. Its subject matter aligns with Decent work and economic growth among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven.</p>",
